{
 "question": "why is app.concurrency set the way it is?",
 "repo": "knadh/listmonk",
 "mode": "both",
 "answer": "`app.concurrency` in `schema.sql` is 10 [dec:knadh/listmonk:config_value:1746b14b6895]. It was set in commit 942eb7c 'Add settings UI and \"hot reload\" support to the app.' by Kailash Nadh on 8 Jul 2020 [commit:knadh/listmonk@942eb7c3d86e]. A recorded handover call confirms it and gives the reason: SES का rate limit hit हो रहा था [dec:knadh/listmonk:kt:507117e52193]. Before it moved to `schema.sql`, `config.toml.sample` had it at 5 (2 Apr 2020) [dec:knadh/listmonk:config_value:ffd03841ed0f] and earlier 100 (25 Oct 2018) [dec:knadh/listmonk:config_value:d3c44eb38b14], until it was removed there on 8 Jul 2020 [dec:knadh/listmonk:config_value:599023a9f988]. Person to ask: Kailash Nadh, who authored 114 of 133 commits on app.concurrency, reviewed 5 of 21 PRs touching it, left 3 review comments on it, stated 5 recorded decisions about it.",
 "refused": false,
